<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cormac's Chapel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1127">1127</a>–1134</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cormac's Chapel is a Romanesque chapel on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rock-of-cashel">Rock of Cashel</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-tipperary">County Tipperary</a>, Ireland, built by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cormac-mac-carthaigh">Cormac Mac Carthaigh</a>, king of Desmond, and consecrated in 1134. With its carved doorways, twin towers and painted interior, it is the finest early Romanesque church in Ireland.</p></div>
